  "Iteration metadata by level. An odd level (and [[0]]) names a metadata frame N//2 climbs up, so [[1]] is the innermost index and [[3]] the enclosing one; an even level names an element frame, where `index` is an ordinary field and reads null.",
  {
    "description": "Depth 2: [[0]] with `index`",
    "rule": {"map": [{"val": "rows"}, {"map": [{"val": "cols"}, {"val": [[0], "index"]}]}]},
    "data": {"tag": "ROOT", "rows": [{"cols": [10, 20, 30]}, {"cols": [40, 50]}]},
    "result": [[0, 1, 2], [0, 1]]
  },
