  "Every frame-pushing operator consumes exactly one level, so from inside its body [[2]] is the enclosing `map` element. `reduce` and a `try` catch arm push frames that carry no iteration metadata, so `index` reads null there while an outer level still reaches the enclosing iterator's index.",
  {
    "description": "filter predicate reads the enclosing map element",
    "rule": {"map": [{"val": "rows"}, {"filter": [{"val": "items"}, {"==": [{"val": [[2], "tag"]}, "R0"]}]}]},
    "data": {"tag": "ROOT", "rows": [{"tag": "R0", "items": [1, 2]}, {"tag": "R1", "items": [3]}]},
    "result": [[1, 2], []]
  },
  {
    "description": "all predicate reads the enclosing map element",
    "rule": {"map": [{"val": "rows"}, {"all": [{"val": "items"}, {"==": [{"val": [[2], "tag"]}, "R0"]}]}]},
    "data": {"tag": "ROOT", "rows": [{"tag": "R0", "items": [1, 2]}, {"tag": "R1", "items": [3]}]},
    "result": [true, false]
  },
  {
    "description": "some predicate reads the enclosing map element",
    "rule": {"map": [{"val": "rows"}, {"some": [{"val": "items"}, {"==": [{"val": [[2], "tag"]}, "R0"]}]}]},
    "data": {"tag": "ROOT", "rows": [{"tag": "R0", "items": [1, 2]}, {"tag": "R1", "items": [3]}]},
    "result": [true, false]
  },
  {
    "description": "none predicate reads the enclosing map element",
    "rule": {"map": [{"val": "rows"}, {"none": [{"val": "items"}, {"==": [{"val": [[2], "tag"]}, "R0"]}]}]},
    "data": {"tag": "ROOT", "rows": [{"tag": "R0", "items": [1, 2]}, {"tag": "R1", "items": [3]}]},
    "result": [false, true]
  },
